        "procedure": "Under dry nitrogen (Schlenk): a 150 mL Schlenk flask with a stir bar was charged with metallic lanthanum (0.93 g, 6.65 mmol), 2-methoxyethanol (10 mL), methanol (10 mL), and MnCl2 (0.42 g, 3.33 mmol). Two crystals of I2 were used to activate metallic lanthanum. The mixture was vigorously stirred at room temperature for 54 h and filtered. The dark brown filtrate was concentrated under vacuum and left at room temperature; colorless crystals of 1 grew in 3–4 weeks, were washed with hexane (3 × 5 mL), and dried under vacuum.",
